gr3d/repos","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/m4gr3d/events{/privacy}","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/m4gr3d/received_events","type":"User","user_view_type":"public","site_admin":false},"author_association":"NONE","issue_field_values":[],"type":null,"active_lock_reason":null,"sub_issues_summary":{"total":0,"completed":0,"percent_completed":0},"issue_dependencies_summary":{"blocked_by":0,"total_blocked_by":0,"blocking":0,"total_blocking":0},"body":"### Tested versions\n\nv4.8.dev4.official [b56a91878]\n\n### System information\n\nGodot v4.8.dev4 - Windows 11 (build 26200) - Multi-window, 1 monitor (1920x1080 @ 120.00 Hz) - Direct3D 12 (Mobile) - dedicated AMD Radeon 780M Graphics (Advanced Micro Devices, Inc.; 32.0.21030.2001) - AMD Ryzen 7 8745HS w/ Radeon 780M Graphics (16 threads) - 31.32 GiB memory - WASAPI (48000 Hz, Stereo/mono)\n\n### Issue description\n\nThe current implementation of Java/Android SDK download is pretty bad as the sub process run by the editor capture the output of what is a standard command line tool which update display using carriage return alone to only print one line updated regularly.\n\nAlthough, each line is captured and added to a sub-window output:\n\n<img width=\"1193\" height=\"348\" alt=\"Image\" src=\"https://github.com/user-attachments/assets/663d93d5-4bec-4f44-b5ec-6b999e43ee63\" />\n\nThis makes the entire editor **unresponsive** (for instance, it took seven seconds to display the main window after being iconified while download is in progress.)\n\nAnd worth, it looks like each output line is dealt one by one, **slowing down the entire download process** leading to very bad download rates.\n(here are _system informer_ performance reports)\n\n<img width=\"753\" height=\"505\" alt=\"Image\" src=\"https://github.com/user-attachments/assets/9707405b-0368-44ab-adc5-46a1cfb15d92\" />\n\n<img width=\"760\" height=\"523\" alt=\"Image\" src=\"https://github.com/user-attachments/assets/66fdeb75-e9cd-4b59-b3d0-727b9515e6bb\" />\n\nGraphics should display a continuous big solid shape not spikes spaced by blanks like this.\nDownloading 50-60 Mb is expected to take more or less **10 mins** ! (on an optic fibre internet connection.)\nFor instance, I just tried this URL (from editor/export/android_sdk_manager.cpp l 424) https://api.adoptium.net/v3/binary/latest/17/ga/windows/x64/jdk/hotspot/normal/eclipse, downloaded **instantly** with Firefox.\n\nAnd the end of the process isn't good too:\n<img width=\"1169\" height=\"582\" alt=\"Image\" src=\"https://github.com/user-attachments/assets/e60e4cff-8399-4ae1-9c31-4203c7956a54\" />\n\nThere is **no output** to check in case of error.\n\n### Steps to reproduce\n\n- create a new project or open an existing one\n- add an Android export presets if none already exists\n- click on the link at the bottom \"Setup Android SDK\" added in this editor release\n\n### Minimal reproduction project (MRP)\n\nN/A","closed_by":null,"reactions":{"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/issues/123359/reactions","total_count":3,"+1":2,"-1":0,"laugh":0,"hooray":0,"confused":0,"heart":0,"rocket":0,"eyes":1},"timeline_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/issues/123359/timeline","performed_via_github_app":null,"state_reason":null,"pinned_comment":null}